/V OPTION CORE IMAGE BINARY LOADER


/THE /V OPTION ALLOWS DEVICE-INDEPENDENT BINARY LOADING
/BY CREATING A CORE IMAGE ON TAPE (OR DISC) OF THE CODE CORRESPONDING
/TO THE AREAS OF CORE FORBIDDEN TO DIRECT LOADING DUE TO
/BOOTSTRAP CONVENTIONS AND THE LOADER ITSELF;ALL OTHER LOCATIONS
/ARE DIRECTLY LOADABLE INCLUDING ALL OF FIELD 1-7 (SOME OTHER SYSTEMS
/RESTRICT LOADING INTO FIELD 1-7 7600-7777)


/THE ONLY RESTRICTION ON LOADING WITH /V IS THAT FIELD 0 7600-7777
/WILL NOT BE LOADED DIRECTLY, HOWEVER THAT CODE WILL
/BE AVAILABLE ON THE SYSTEM DEVICE (UNIT 0 BLOCK BINBLK+24) AS A RELIC FOR
/FURTHER LOADING IF DESIRED;USE THE FOLLOWING CODING TO LOAD IT

/       COUNT,  7600                    /CLA
/               TAD I   (7605)          /GET SYS LOAD FUNCTION WORD
/               AND     (7)             /JUST UNIT BITS
/               TAD     FUN             /ADD ON 1 BLOCK READ
/               DCA     FUN             /SAVE INLINE
/               TAD I   (7606)          /GET SYS LOAD BLOCK NUMBER
/               TAD     BLKNO           /ADD ON OFFSET
/               DCA     BLKNO           /SAVE INLINE
/               JMS I   (7640)          /SYSTEM I/O ENTRY
/       CORE,   UCORE                   /USER'S 1 PAGE BUFFER
/       FUN,    1^100+.-.               /READ 1 BLOCK
/       BLKNO,  .-.+12                  /WHERE CODE IS
/               TAD I   CORE            /GET A WORD
/               DCA I   COUNT           /PUT IT
/               ISZ     CORE            /BUMP POINTER
/               ISZ     COUNT           /BUMP IT AND COUNT
/               JMP     .-4             /GO BACK AND DO IT AGAIN 'TIL DONE
/
/THIS COMPLETES LOADING OF 7600 FIELD 0
/NOTICE THAT THIS REQUIRES A 1 PAGE BUFFER ANYWHERE IN FIELD 0
/(APPROPRIATE CHANGES FOR FIELDS OTHER THAN ZERO CAN BE MADE)
/THE SYSTEM I/O ROUTINES ARE DESTROYED IN THE PROCESS AS THEY
/ARE THE FORMER OCCUPANTS OF 7600 FIELD ZERO!
/
/NOTE: IT IS POSSIBLE TO OVERLAY THE SYSTEM I/O ROUTINES DIRECTLY
/BUT THIS IS TO BE DISCOURAGED BY ANYONE OTHER THAN A 
/P?S SYSTEMS PROGRAMMER THOROUGHLY FAMILIAR WITH THE PARTICULAR COPY
/OF THE SYSTEM I/O ROUTINES IN USE AT THE TIME AS ANY OTHER ATTEMPT
/TO DO THIS WILL MOST CERTAINLY FAIL.(THIS DOES NOT IMPLY THAT A
/P?S SYSTEMS PROGRAMMER WILL NECESSARILY SUCCEED! (MARIO'S NOTE, ED.))










