/P?S MONITOR SYSTEM I/O
 
/THE NEW IMPROVED P?S MONITOR SYSTEM'S I/O ROUTINES
/FOR ALL SUPPORTED MASS STORAGE DEVICES
/INCLUDES SYSIO, BOOTSTRAP RECORD, SYSTEM LOADER, FILE AND PARAMETER AREA
/RL (ROTH-LASNER) VERSION FOR USE IN FIELD 0 LOCATION 7600 ONLY
 
 
 
/       CALLING SEQUENCE:
/       JMS I   (7640)          /SZA CLA IS CONVENIENT
/       CORE                    /CORE ADDRESS
/       FUNCTION                /FUNCTION WORD
/       BLOCK                   /STARTING BLOCK NUMBER
/       RETURNS TO HERE         /RETURN ADDRESS
 
/FUNCTION WORD IS AS FOLLOWS:
/<BIT 0>        <BITS 1-5>      <BITS 6-8>      <BITS 9-11>
/ READ            NUMBER          FIELD            UNIT
/  OR               OF              OF              TO
/ WRITE           BLOCKS         TRANSFER           USE
 
/A ZERO BLOCK COUNT IS ASSUMED TO BE A 40 THUS
/TRANSFERRING AN ENTIRE MEMORY FIELD
 
/THE DATA FIELD UPON ENTRY WILL BE ASSUMED TO BE THE CALLING
/FIELD, SO TRANSFERS CALLED FROM EXTENDED MEMORY SHOULD
/BE PRECEDED BY:
/       CDF     THISFIELD       /(IF NECESSARY)
/       CIF     00              /SYSIO'S FIELD
 
/THE INSTRUCTION AND DATA FIELD WILL BE THAT OF THE CALLER'S
/UPON RETURNING SUCESSFULLY FROM THE CALL TO SYSIO
 
/BOOTSTRAPPING IS PERFORMED BY BRANCHING TO FIELD 0 LOCATION 7600
/THE AC AND LINK ARE ARBITRARY AT THIS TIME
/AS THEY ARE DESTROYED. IF INTERRUPT IS ON, A
/LONGER (IN TIME) BOOTSTRAP MAY OCCUR BUT IS OTHERWISE HARMLESS
 
/ERROR RECOVERY USUALLY CONSISTS OF HALTING THE CPU WITH
/APPROPRIATE ERROR STATUS BITS IN THE AC IF APPLICABLE
/HITTING CONTINUE WILL CAUSE A RETRY OF THE I/O OPERATION
/USUALLY IN ITS ENTIRETY

        FIELD   0               /ENSURE FIELD 0

        *7400                   /GENERATE THE HANDLERS HERE

GENAD1, NOPUNCH                 /FOOL THE ASSEMBLER

        *7600                   /WHERE THEY ULTIMATELY GO

        ENPUNCH                 /RESUME BINARY OUTPUT
        XLIST   OFF
        IFNZRO  IPB     <
        XLIST   ON
SBOOT,  JMS     SYSIO           /CALL I/O TO BOOTSTRAP
S7600,  7600                    /READ INTO 7600
        20^100                  /READ IN FIRST 20 BLOCKS
        0                       /START AT BLOCK 0
SWAL,   .-.                     /SWITCHES /A-/L
SWMX,   .-.                     /SWITCHES /M-/X
SWY9,   .-.                     /SWITCHES /Y-/9
SOUTFLS,.-.                     /OUTPUT FILE COUNT
SDATE,  .-.                     /SYSTEM DATE WORD
SCRSIZE,.-.                     /SOFT CORE SIZE WORD
 
SERR,   HLT                     /SHOW THEM THE PARITY ERROR
        NL7775                  /BACKUP 3
        JMP     SRETRY          /TRY, TRY AGAIN
 
SRCV,   CLA                     /CLEAN UP
        RSKF                    /ANYTHING IN YET?
        JMP     .-1             /NO, WAIT
        RRBC                    /YES, HERE IT IS
        JMP I   SWAIT           /RETURN
 
SWAIT,  .-.                     /WAIT ROUTINE
        CLL                     /MAKE SURE
        TAD     SDIR            /PUT DIRECTION
        TAD     SDIR            /INTO LINK
        SZL                     /TRANSMIT
        JMP     SRCV            /NO, RECEIVE
        JMP     SAGN            /YES, GO TRANSMIT IT
 
SFUNCT, 20^100                  /FUNCTION WORD
 
SLOAD,  JMS     SYSIO           /READ IN SYSTEM PROGRAM
SCORE,  0                       /CORE ARGUMENT
SFUN,   WRITE                   /DEFAULT IS TO SAVE ALL OF CORE
SBLOCK, BINADR                  /USE DEFAULT FILES
        JMP I   SYSTART         /NOW START IT UP
SYSTART,SBOOT                   /THROUGH HERE
SYSIO,  SPARM                   /I/O ENTRY
        NL0002                  /SET CIF BITS
        RDF                     /GET CALLING FIELD
        TAD     SCDF            /MAKE IT CIF CDF CALLER
        DCA     SOUT            /SAVE FOR LATER
SRETRY, TAD     SYSIO           /AC=-3 IF RETRYING
        DCA     SYSIO           /UPDATE
        DCA     SDIR            /SET TRANSMIT DIRECTION
        JMS     SWAIT           /START UP A TRANSMISSION REQUEST
        RRBS                    /CLEAR READ FLAG NOW
        STA                     /SETUP INITIALIZE OPERATION
        JMS     SWAIT           /GO SEND IT
        AND I   SYSIO           /GET CORE ARGUMENT
        DCA     SBUFF           /SAVE IT
        ISZ     SYSIO           /BUMP TO FUNCTION WORD
        TAD I   SYSIO           /GET FUNCTION
        JMS     SWAIT           /TRANSMIT IT
        DCA     SFUNCT          /SAVE IT FOR LATER
        ISZ     SYSIO           /BUMP TO BLOCK NUMBER
        TAD I   SYSIO           /GET BLOCK NUMBER
        JMS     SWAIT           /TRANSMIT IT
        CLA                     /CLEAN UP
        ISZ     SYSIO           /BUMP TO FINAL REWARD
        TAD     SFUNCT          /GET FUNCTION WORD
        AND     S70             /JUST FIELD BITS
        TAD     SCDF            /MAKE INTO CDF BUFFER
        DCA     SWC             /PUT INLINE
        TAD     SFUNCT          /GET FUNCTION WORD AGAIN
        RAL                     /R/W TO LINK
        AND     S7600           /ISOLATE PAGE BITS
        SZA                     /FULL CALL?
        CIA                     /NO, INVERT
SWC,    .&177+4000              /EXECUTE CDF BUFFER;ALSO WORD COUNT
        DCA     SWC             /SAVE AS WORD COUNT
        DCA     SCHECK          /ZERO CHECKSUM
        CML RAR                 /INVERT AND MOVE R/W
        DCA     SDIR            /SAVE AS TRANSFER DIRECTION
SLOOP,  TAD I   SBUFF           /GET A WORD
        JMS     SWAIT           /READ OR WRITE IT
SWAIT2, DCA I   SBUFF           /PUT A WORD
        TAD I   SBUFF           /GET IT BACK
        TAD     SCHECK          /UPDATE CHECKSUM
        DCA     SCHECK          /SAVE IT
        ISZ     SBUFF           /BUMP TO NEXT
S70,    70                      /JUST IN CASE
        ISZ     SWC             /DONE YET?
        JMP     SLOOP           /NO, GO BACK
        TAD     SCHECK          /GET CHECKSUM
        CIA                     /INVERT IT
        JMS     SWAIT           /SEND IT
        TAD     SCHECK          /COMPARE IT
SOUT,   CIF CDF 00              /BACK TO CALLING FIELD
        CLL                     /CLEAN UP
        CLA/SNA                 /SKIP ON PARITY ERROR
        JMP I   SYSIO           /RETURN
        CIF     00              /QUICK BEFORE IT MELTS
        JMP     SERR            /BARF
 
SAGN,   TBLS                    /SEND IT
        TSKF                    /READY?
        JMP     .-1             /NO, WAIT
        SNL                     /HAVE WE BEEN HERE BEFORE
        SZA                     /SHOULD WE COME AGAIN?
        JMP I   SWAIT           /NO, GO BACK TO WHERE YOU ONCE BELONGED
        STL                     /DO IT AGAIN
        JMP     SAGN            /FOR REDUNDANCY
 
SCDF,   CDF                     /CONSTANT 6201
SCHECK, .-.                     /CHECKSUM TEMPORARY
SDIR,   4000                    /TRANSFER DIRECTION
SBUFF,  .                       /CORE BUFFER POINTER
 
        ZBLOCK  7756-.          /EMPTY SPACE
 
SPARM,  TAD     SSNA            /EQUALS PARAMETER WORD
SFILES, DCA     SOUT+2          /FILE ARGUMENTS START HERE
        JMP I   .+1             /START IT UP
        INPBUF                  /THROUGH HERE

SBOOT2, TAD     S4200           /SETUP THE
        DCA     SWC             /WORD COUNT
        DCA     SBUFF           /AND TRANSFER ADDRESS
        JMP     SLOOP           /KEEP GOING

SSNA,   SNA                     /INSTRUCTION CONSTANT
S4200,  4200                    /WORD COUNT CONSTANT

        ZBLOCK  -.              /EMPTY SPACE

/       INTERPROCESSOR BUFFER DEFINITIONS
 
        IPRCOD= 6620            /INTERPROCESSOR RECEIVE CODE
        IPTCOD= 6630            /INTERPROCESSOR TRANSMIT CODE
        RSKF=   IPRCOD+1        /SKIP ON RECEIVE FLAG
        RTIE=   IPRCOD+2        /SET/CLEAR INTERRUPT ENABLE PER AC[11]
        RRBS=   IPRCOD+4        /READ RECEIVE BUFFER STATIC, CLEAR RECEIVE FLAG
        RRBC=   IPRCOD+6        /READ RECEIVE BUFFER, CLEAR RECEIVE FLAG, SET TRANSMIT FLAG
        TSKF=   IPTCOD+1        /SKIP ON TRANSMIT FLAG
        TCLF=   IPTCOD+2        /CLEAR TRANSMIT BUFFER, CLEAR TRANSMIT FLAG
        TLBC=   IPTCOD+4        /OR AC WITH TRANSMIT BUFFER
        TBLS=   IPTCOD+6        /LOAD TRANSMIT BUFFER, CLEAR TRANSMIT FLAG
        XLIST   OFF             >
        XLIST   OFF
        IFNZRO  DYNEX   <
        XLIST   ON
SBOOT,  JMS     SYSIO           /CALL I/O ROUTINES TO BOOT
S7600,  7600                    /READ INTO 7600
SBUNIT, BTUNIT                  /20 BLOCKS IS ENOUGH
        0000                    /FROM BLOCK 0
SWAL,   .-.                     /SWITCHES /A-/L
SWMX,   JMP     S7600&177+1     /SWITCHES /M-/X
SWY9,   .-.                     /SWITCHES /Y-/9
SOUTFLS,JMP     SPARM&177+1     /NUMBER OF OUTPUT FILES
SDATE,  .-.                     /SYSTEM DATE WORD
SCRSIZE,.-.                     /SOFTWARE CORE SIZE

S4070,  4070                    /CONSTANT 4070
SBFPTR, SBUF+2                  /COMMAND POINTER AND FILE MODE BIT

SWAIT,  SWAITR                  /DISK WAIT ROUTINE
SWTAGN, DEXC                    /GO DO SPECIFIED FUNCTION
        DSBY                    /WAIT 'TIL CONTROLLER
        JMP     .-1             /IS FREE AGAIN
        TAD     STATUS          /GET DISK STATUS
        AND     S4077           /JUST BAD BITS
        SNA                     /SKIP ON ANY ERROR
        JMP I   SWAIT           /RETURN IF ALL OK
SERR,   HLT                     /LET THEM SEE THE PROBLEM
        AND     S40             /RECALIBRATE NEEDED?
        SNA                     /SKIP IF SO
        JMP     SWTAGN          /JUMP IF NOT
        JMP     SRETRY          /RECALIBRATE THERE

SFUNCT, 20^100                  /FUNCTION WORD STORED HERE
 
SLOAD,  JMS     SYSIO           /SYSTEM LOADER;DEFAULT IS TO SAVE CORE
SCORE,  0                       /CORE ARGUMENT
SFUN,   WRITE                   /NUMBER OF BLOCKS TO READ OR WRITE, FIELD, UNIT
SBLOCK, BINADR                  /STARTING BLOCK NUMBER
        JMP I   SYSTART         /STARTING AT
SYSTART,SBOOT                   /THIS ADDRESS
/I/O ROUTINES ENTER HERE
SYSIO,  .-.                     /I/O ENTRY POINT
        STA                     /BACKUP
        TAD I   SYSIO           /GET CORE ADDRESS
        DCA     SCAA            /PUT INTO COMMAND
        RDF                     /GET CALLING FIELD
        TAD     S6202           /MAKE IT A CIF CALLER
        DCA     SEXIT           /PUT INTO EXIT ROUTINE
        ISZ     SYSIO           /BUMP TO FUNCTION WORD
        TAD I   SYSIO           /GET THE FUNCTION
        DCA     SFUNCT          /SAVE FOR EVERYONE
        ISZ     SYSIO           /BUMP TO BLOCK NUMBER
SRETRY, SNA CLA                 /SKIP IF RECALIBRATE NEEDED
        JMP     SNORM           /JUMP IF NORMAL CALL OR RETRY
        TAD     S300            /GET RETRY FUNCTION
        DCA     SBUF2           /SET IT UP
        JMS     SWAIT           /TRY TO RECALIBRATE
SNORM,  TAD     SFUNCT          /GET FUNCTION WORD
        RAL                     /MOVE LEFT
        AND     S7600           /ISOLATE PAGE BITS
        CIA                     /WANT NEGATIVE FORM
        DCA     SWC             /PUT INTO COMMAND
        DCON                    /USE PHYSICAL UNIT 0
        TAD     SBFPTR          /SET UP
        DLBP                    /COMMAND POINTER
        TAD I   SYSIO           /GET BLOCK NUMBER
        CLL RAR                 /%2
        CLL RAR                 /%4
        DYNFIX-1&1^CML CLL RAR  /%8
        DCA     SBUF            /SAVE THERE FOR NOW
        TAD I   SYSIO           /GET BLOCK NUMBER AGAIN
S300,   AND     S7              /JUST LOW SECTOR BITS
        DCA     STEMP1          /SAVE FOR LATER
S7,     7                       /CONSTANT 0007
        TAD     SFUNCT          /GET FUNCTION AGAIN
        RAR                     /LOW ORDER TO LINK
        CLA RAR                 /UNIT NOW IN AC[0]
        DCA     STEMP2          /SAVE IT
        TAD     SFUNCT          /GET FUNCTION AGAIN
        AND     S4070           /L  W 0 0 0 0 0 F F F 0 0 0
        SPA                     /READING?
        TAD     S6000           /NO, FIXUP WRITE
        TAD     STEMP2          /L  U W 0 0 0 0 F F F 0 0 0
        CLL RAL                 /U  W 0 0 0 0 F F F 0 0 0 0
        TAD     STEMP1          /U  W 0 0 0 0 F F F 0 S S S
        RTR                     /S  S U W 0 0 0 0 F F F 0 S
        RTR                     /0  S S S U W 0 0 0 0 F F F
        DCA     SBUF2           /SET UP COMMAND
        TAD     SFUNCT          /GET FUNCTION AGAIN
        RTR                     /MOVE UNIT BITS
        RAR                     /UNIT[9] TO LINK, UNIT[10] TO BIT[0]
        SPA CLA                 /HALF UNIT?
        TAD     S626            /YES
        SZL                     /UPPER UNIT?
        TAD     S1454           /YES
        TAD     SBUF            /ADD ON TRUNCATED BLOCK NUMBER
        DCA     SBUF            /SETUP COMMAND WORD
        JMS     SWAIT           /GO TO IT
S40,    ISZ     SYSIO           /BUMP PAST BLOCK NUMBER
SEXIT,  CIF     00              /GOTO CALLING FIELD
        JMP I   SYSIO           /RETURN
 
S6000,  6000                    /CONSTANT 6000
S626,   626                     /CONSTANT 0626
S1454,  1454                    /CONSTANT 1454
S6202,  6202                    /CONSTANT 6202
/THE FOLLOWING MUST BE AT 7740
SBUF,   0                       /DISK, CYLINDER, HEAD, HIGH SECTOR
SBUF2,  0                       /LOW SECTOR, OPCODE, CHAIN, INTERRUPT, EXTENDED MEMORY
SWC,    20^200                  /WORD COUNT
SCAA,   SBOOT-1                 /CURRENT ADDRESS
S4077,  4077                    /CONSTANT NOT TOUCHED BY HARDWARE
STEMP1, .-.                     /RETURNED ADDRESS AFTER TRANSFER
STEMP2, .-.                     /ZEROED BY HARDWARE
STATUS, .-.                     /STATUS AFTER TRANSFER

        ZBLOCK  7756-.          /EMPTY SPACE
 
SPARM,  CLA+400                 /CLEAN UP
SFILES, TAD     SBOOT&177+1     /GET A WORD
        DCA I   SPARM&177+1     /PUT A WORD
        ISZ     SFILES&177+1    /BUMP TO NEXT
        ISZ     SPARM&177+1     /ANY MORE?
        JMP     SFILES&177+1    /YES, GO BACK
        JMP I   S7600&177+1     /NO, GO BOOTSTRAP FOR REAL

SWAITR, TAD     SBUNIT          /GET FUNCTION WORD TO BOOTSTRAP
        DCA     UNIT            /SAVE IN MONITOR
        TAD     UNIT            /RETRIEVE UNIT
        DCA     OLDUNIT         /SAVE FOR BENEFIT OF OVERLAYS
        JMP I   .+1             /NOW START IT UP
        INPBUF                  /THROUGH HERE

        ZBLOCK  -.              /EMPTY SPACE

/DYNEX/DSD-240-8 DEFINITIONS
 
        DEVCOD= 0620            /DEVICE CODE OF CONTROLLER
        DTST=   6000+DEVCOD     /READ TEST STATUS
        DSKF=   6001+DEVCOD     /SKIP ON DONE
        DCLF=   6002+DEVCOD     /CLEAR DONE FLAG
        DSBY=   6003+DEVCOD     /SKIP ON CONTROLLER BUSY
        DEXC=   6004+DEVCOD     /EXECUTE COMMAND BUFFER
        DLBP=   6005+DEVCOD     /LOAD BUFFER POINTER REGISTER
        DRDS=   6006+DEVCOD     /READ STATUS
        DCON=   6007+DEVCOD     /LOAD CONTROL REGISTER
        XLIST   OFF     >
        XLIST   OFF
        IFNZRO  RX8B+RX8BH      <
        XLIST   ON
/P?S DEC-COMPATIBLE FLOPPY DISC HANDLER.

/A HANDLER FOR THAT BLECHEROUS PIECE OF HARDWARE, THE DEC VERSION OF THE
/IBM-COMPATIBLE FLOPPY DISC AND ANY OTHER DISC INTERFACE TO A PDP-8 TYPE MACHINE
/FOOLISHLY DESIGNED TO BE COMPATIBLE WITH IT!
 
/GENERAL WARNING TO ANYONE FOOLISH ENOUGH TO WRITE CODE FOR THIS HUNK OF JUNK:
/THE HARDWARE IS SO INCREDIBLY CRUDE THAT STRANGE OPERATIONS MUST BE PERFORMED
/ON THIS DEVICE TO GET THE HANDLER TO FIT EVEN THOUGH DISC THROUGHPUT AND ERROR
/HANDLING ARE GROSSLY INEFFICIENT. THIS DEVICE IS CRUMMY TO THE POINT OF INSULT!
 
/WORDS TO THE WISE:
 
/       A)      THE COLD BOOTSTRAP CONVENTION HEREIN DESCRIBED IS DESIGNED TO
/               BE FORGIVING TO ANY OPERATING SYSTEM, NOT LIKE DEC'S WHICH
/               NEARLY LOCKS YOU INTO A SYSTEM AS WARPED IN DESIGN AS OS/8.
/       B)      A STAND-ALONE PROGRAM MUST INITIALIZE TRACK 0 TO THE SECONDARY
/               BOOTSTRAP DESCRIBED BELOW BEFORE A COLD BOOTSTRAP CAN BE
/               ATTEMPTED, HOWEVER THIS NEED BE DONE ONLY ONCE, EVEN WHEN
/               SWITCHING OPERATING SYSTEMS WRITTEN ON THE DEVICE (SUCH AS
/               P?S/8, POLY BASIC, LASNER'S BETTER OS/8 VERSION, ETC.) AS ALL
/               SYSTEMS WILL EASILY BECOME COMPATIBLE WITH THIS BOOTSTRAP WHICH
/               BEHAVES ACCORDING TO THE TRADITIONAL PDP-8 CONVENTION (LOGICAL
/               BLOCK 0 LOADS INTO 07600).
/       C)      DEC'S OS/8 VERSION AND THE P?S RX8BX SYSTEM WILL RUN UNHAMPERED
/               BY THE MODIFIED CONTENTS OF TRACK 0 (THEY DON'T USE IT).
/       D)      THE COLD BOOTSTRAP CONVENTION IS VERY SIMILAR TO THE ORIGINAL
/               DEC OS/8 BOOTSTRAP TO ALLOW VARIOUS BOOTSTRAP LOADERS (MI-8/E,
/               MI-8/A, IM6100 FIRM-WARE LOADERS, ETC.) TO EASILY SUPPORT ANY
/               SYSTEM (ISZ'ING A LOCATION IN THIS BOOTSTRAP MAKES IT BOOT DEC'S
/               OS/8 VERSION AND THE P?S RX8BX SYSTEM; LEAVING IT ALONE BOOTS
/               EVERYTHING ELSE, INCLUDING THE LASNER-IMPROVED OS/8 VERSION, SO
/               FIRMWARE ROUTINES CAN DECIDE UPON WHICH SYSTEM TO BOOTSTRAP).
/       E)      MANUAL BOOTSTRAP CODE TO BOOTSTRAP ONLY UNIT 0 CAN BE TOGGLED
/               IN BY HAND.
/       F)      A LONG COLD START BOOTSTRAP CAN BE DEFINED TO BE READ IN ON
/               PAPER-TAPE, PREFERABLY IN SLIM FORMAT WHOSE LOADER IS ITSELF
/               SHORTER THAN ANY POSSIBLE DIRECT MANUAL BOOTSTRAP.
/       G)      THE P?S/8, POLY BASIC AND LASNER-IMPROVED OS/8 SYSTEMS REQUIRE
/               ADDITIONAL HARDWARE/FIRMWARE TO OPERATE AT ALL IN THE 4K
/               UNRESTRICTED VERSION WHICH CAN BE IMPLEMENTED AS AN OMNIBUS
/               PERIPHERAL QUITE READILY, OR AS AN IM6100 PERIPHERAL EITHER FULLY
/               IN HARDWARE OR MOSTLY IN CONTROL-PANEL FIRMWARE. IN EITHER CASE,
/               THE HANDLER AND LOADER DEPEND ON THIS HARDWARE/FIRMWARE FOR
/               PROPER OPERATION IN THE UNRESTRICTED SYSTEM;THE SOFTWARE CORE
/               SIZE LIMITED SYSTEMS WILL OF COURSE NEED EXTENDED MEMORY AND NO
/               ADDITIONAL HARDWARE FOR HANDLER AND LOADER OPERATION.
/       H)      AS OF THE PRESENT IMPLEMENTATION, AN 8/I TYPE PROCESSOR OR
/               BETTER IS NEEDED TO RUN THIS HANDLER. THIS IS NOT EXPECTED TO BE
/               A PROBLEM AS ECO'S EXIST TO UPDATE PDP-8'S TO DO COMBINED IAC AND
/               ROTATE INSTRUCTIONS (N. B. A DW-8/E, THE ADDITIONAL HARDWARE,
/               AND ALL OTHER RELATED ECO'S ARE PREREQUISITE FOR RUNNING THIS
/               HANDLER ON AN RX8B OR EQUIVALENT ON A PRE-OMNIBUS MACHINE!).
/       I)      SEE RX8BX LISTING FOR MORE CHOICE WORDS ABOUT THIS IDIOCY!
        XLIST   OFF             >
        XLIST   OFF
        IFNZRO  RX8BX   <
        XLIST   ON
/P?S DEC-COMPATIBLE FLOPPY DISC HANDLER.
 
/A HANDLER FOR THAT BLECHEROUS PIECE OF HARDWARE, THE DEC VERSION OF THE
/IBM-COMPATIBLE FLOPPY DISC, AND ANY OTHER DISC INTERFACE TO A PDP-8 TYPE
/MACHINE FOOLISHLY DESIGNED TO BE COMPATIBLE WITH IT!
 
/GENERAL WARNING TO ANYONE FOOLISH ENOUGH TO WRITE CODE FOR THIS HUNK OF JUNK:
/THE HARDWARE IS SO INCREDIBLY CRUDE THAT STRANGE OPERATIONS MUST BE PERFORMED
/ON THIS DEVICE TO GET THE HANDLER TO FIT EVEN THOUGH DISC THROUGHPUT AND
/ERROR HANDLING ARE GROSSLY INEFFICIENT.
/THE BOOTSTRAP FOR THIS DEVICE COMES FROM DEC. IT WAS WRITTEN SELFISHLY IN SUCH
/A WAY THAT ONLY A SYSTEM SUCH AS OS/8 COULD NOT BE HAMPERED BY IT (ONE MINOR
/ADVANTAGE OF OS/8 OVER OTHER PDP-8 BASED SYSTEMS IS THAT IT HAS A DEFINED
/BOOTSTRAP ONLY (NEARLY) BLOCK WHICH CAN FIXUP FOR THE MOST BIZARRE
/BOOTSTRAPPING CONVENTIONS). SINCE P?S/8 IS SIMILAR TO THE MORE TRADITIONAL
/PDP-8 BASED SYSTEMS IN ITS BOOTSTRAP CONVENTION, IT, AS WELL AS THE OTHER
/(DEC) SYSTEMS, SUFFERS FROM THE ILLS OF THIS UNWISE STANDARD. THE OTHER
/PDP-8 SYSTEMS ARE THUS LOCKED OUT; P?S/8 WILL SURVIVE IF THIS HANDLER IS USED,
/EVEN THOUGH THE HANDLER IS DRASTICALLY WEAKENED BY THE STRANGE BOOTSTRAP
/(AT FIRST, NOT ALL OF EVEN THE FIRST HALF OF THE FIRST PAGE OF THE HANDLER
/COMES INTO CORE!). IF ABSOLUTE DEC BOOTSTRAP COMPATIBILITY IS NOT REQUIRED,
/SEE THE OTHER RX01 HANDLERS WHICH UTILIZE A SANE BOOTSTRAP APPROACH (WHICH
/CAN ALSO BE USED WITH A SANER OS/8 BOOTSTRAP AS WELL!).

/THE RX01 INTERFACE, EVEN THOUGH IT IS A MICRO-PROCESSOR BASED CONTROLLER,
/DOES NOT DO ANY ERROR RECOVERY FOR YOU. IN ADDITION, THE INDIVIDUAL ERRORS
/CANNOT BE SENSED WITHIN THE HANDLER DUE TO LACK OF SPACE. THE ONLY POSSIBLE
/ERROR RECOVERY IS TO "INIT" THE DRIVES, WHICH DESTROYS THE SILO (WHY?) IN THE
/PROCESS. UNLESS THE SILO IS RELOADED BEFORE RETRYING TO WRITE OUT THE CURRENT
/SECTOR, THE CURRENT SECTOR WILL WIND UP BEING A COPY OF TRACK 1, SECTOR 1!
/THE CURRENT DESIRED (CORE) CONTENTS WILL BE LOST AND NO ERRORS WILL EVER BE
/DETECTED, EVEN WHEN READING IT BACK LATER (ONLY A DIRECT WRITE/READ VERIFY
/OPERATION WOULD BE SAFE THROUGH THIS OPERATION; OS/8, P?S/8, AND MOST OF THE
/OTHER PDP-8 BASED SYSTEMS DON'T USUALLY DO THIS!). THIS HANDLER (THROUGH MUCH
/SQUEEZING) WILL NOT HAVE THIS PROBLEM AS ON ANY ERROR, THE ENTIRE I/O
/TRANSACTION IS REPEATED (UGH!), EVEN THOUGH IT: A) MAY HAVE BEEN ONLY A READ,
/B) ONLY ONE SECTOR MAY HAVE HAD TO BE RETRIED. THIS IS STILL BETTER THAN BEING
/UNCERTAIN OF THE RELIABILITY OF THE WRITTEN DATA!

/THE RX01 IS TOO SLOW TO TRANSFER CONTIGUOUS SECTORS, SO AN INTERLEAVING SCHEME
/IS USED. DEC UNWISELY CHOSE TO ARBITRATE THE USE OF NON-INTERLEAVED IBM FORMAT
/AS THEIR STANDARD FOR ALL USES EVEN THOUGH IBM ITSELF ALLOWS FOR INTERLEAVING,
/AND IN ANY CASE STAND-ALONE PROGRAMS COULD HAVE WRITTEN IBM COMPATIBLE DATA
/ANYWAY IF ANYONE CARED! THUS DEC FORCES YOU TO SOFTWARE INTERLEAVE THE
/NON-INTERLEAVED SECTORS. THE SIMPLEST APPROACH TO THIS INTERLEAVING ALGORITHM
/IS TO USE CORRECTED REPETITIVE SUBTRACTING, HOWEVER THIS LEADS TO A FAILURE TO
/KEEP IN STEP WITH THE TWO-WAY INTERLEAVED SECTORS WHEN ACCESSING THE HIGHER
/TRACKS, ESPECIALLY ON THE SLOWER CPU'S (IM6100 BASED). THIS LEADS TO
/THROUGHPUT DEGRADED BY A FACTOR OF 13! THIS APPROACH IS THE ONE THAT DEC USES
/WITHIN OS/8 AS THEY HAVE NO OTHER CHOICE (IN 8K) BUT TO USE THE SMALLEST PIECE
/OF CODE. THIS HANDLER USES A HIGH-SPEED ALGORITHM TO ALLOW EVEN THE SLOWEST
/CPU TO KEEP UP WITH THE TWO-WAY INTERLEAVE.

/THE PRICE PAID FOR ALL OF THESE FEATURES IS THE NEED FOR EXTENDED MEMORY (THIS
/IS A SOFTWARE CORE SIZE-LIMITED HANDLER).
        XLIST   OFF     >
