/SYKES 7X50 HANDLER FOR P?S/8

/THIS HANDLER REQUIRES THE USE OF A HELPER FIELD PAGE 7600 TO PERFORM THE
/FUNCTIONS REQUIRED BY A P?S SYSTEM HANDLER AND TO FACILITATE THE WRITING
/OF A SLURP LOADER. THE PACKING ALGORITHM USED IS THE SAME AS THAT OF THE
/STANDARD SYKES OS/8 HANDLER, SO THAT THE P?S/8 - OS/8 CONVERSION PROGRAM
/("CONVRT") MAY BE USED WITH NO RESTRICTIONS.

/SOME NOTES ABOUT THE SYKES 7X50 INTERFACE:
/THERE ARE SEVERAL PROBLEMS GENERATED BY THE PDP-8 INTERFACE FOR THE OTHERWISE
/QUITE ACCEPTABLE 7000 SERIES FLOPPY DISKS. THE BIGGEST PROBLEM IS THAT THERE
/ARE ONLY 3 IOT'S THAT TRY TO PERFORM 5 DISTINCT FUNCTIONS, AND ONLY MANAGE IT
/BY A KLUDGE. PRIMARILY, TO ISSUE A COMMAND, ONE MUST GIVE THE "SFWR"
/INSTRUCTION WITH BIT 3 SET AND THE LOW-ORDER 8 BITS ENCODED AS NECESSARY.
/TO OUTPUT A DATA BYTE TO THE 7000, BIT 3 MUST BE CLEAR! (THIS CAUSES MANY
/HEADACHES, SINCE UNPACKING ALGORITHMS TEND TO LEAVE "UNIMPORTANT" BITS DIRTY).
/AN ANALOGOUS SITUATION ARISES WITH THE "SFRD" IOT.  IF BIT 3 IS SET, IT IS
/INTERPRETED AS READ STATUS (OR'ED INTO THE AC), AND IF IT IS CLEAR, IT IS A
/READ DATA (ALSO OR'ED IN).
/THE FOLLOWING IS THE COLD-START BOOTSTRAP CODE WHICH MUST BE TOGGLED IN VIA
/WHATEVER FRONT PANEL HARDWARE THE USER MAY HAVE. IF DESIRED, THE STANDARD
/SYKES 7X50 OS/8 BOOTSTRAP OR THE PDP-8/A "SW" ROM MAY BE USED INSTEAD.

        NOPUNCH                 /DON'T LOAD THIS CODE

        *07752                  /IT'S FOR INFORMATION ONLY!

MN401,  0401                    /HARMLESS AND
MNBPTR, 0                       /LIKEWISE
MANBUT, TAD     MN401           /SETUP TRACK AND SECTOR VALUE
        SFWR                    /ISSUE THE TRACK SELECT
        SFWR                    /AND READ SECTOR 1
MNBCTR, SBOOT                   /CLEAN UP
MNLOOP, SFSF                    /DATA SERVICE FLAG UP?
        JMP     MNLOOP          /NO, WAIT FOR IT
        SFRD                    /YES, READ IN A BYTE
        CLL RTL                 /MOVE IT OVER
        CLL RTL                 /INTO HIGH ORDER 8 BITS
        DCA     MANBUT          /SAVE TEMPORARILY
        SFSF                    /WAIT FOR NEXT BYTE
        JMP     .-1             /AS LONG AS NECESSARY
        SFRD                    /GET NEXT BYTE INTO AC
        RTR                     /MOVE TO LOW ORDER
        RTR                     /4 BITS OF WORD
        TAD     MANBUT          /PACK WITH OTHER PIECE
        DCA I   MNBPTR          /STORE A WORD
        ISZ     MNBPTR          /BUMP TO NEXT
        ISZ     MNBCTR          /BUMP THE COUNT
        JMP     MNLOOP          /BACK FOR MORE
/WILL FALL THROUGH AND BEGIN SECONDARY BOOTSTRAP HERE AT 00000

        *7600                   /RESTORE ORIGIN

        ENPUNCH                 /RE-ENABLE BINARY OUTPUT
SBOOT,  JMP     SBUTMR&177      /"JMS SYSIO" AT RUN-TIME
