/THE FOLLOWING CODE IS ENTERED AT COLD START TIME ONLY. IT'S PURPOSE IS TO LOAD
/BLOCK 74 (H7600-H7777 CONTENTS) INTO 07600-07777. THIS CODE (BLOCK 0 CONTENTS)
/IS EXECUTED IN 00000-00177 (WHERE IT WAS LOADED BY THE MANUAL BOOT). CODE
/RESIDING IN 07600 (HELPER FIELD CONTENTS) THEN MOVES ITSELF INTO FIELD
/HFIELD%10, THEN BRANCHES TO MORE OF ITSELF (SEE LATER COMMENTS).

SBUTMR, TAD     S437&177        /GET TRACK SELECT COMMAND
SPARM,  TAD     S7746&177       /ADJUST TO TRACK 5
SFILES, SFWR                    /DO IT
        TAD     S14&177         /SELECT SECTOR 21 COMMAND NOW IN AC
        SFWR                    /DO IT
BT2PTR, SBOOT                   /CLEAN UP
BT2LUP, JMS     SGTBYTE&177     /GET A BYTE
        CLL RTL                 /PACK IN STANDARD
        CLL RTL                 /SYKES FORMAT
        DCA     SPARM&177       /SAVE TEMPORARILY
        JMS     SGTBYTE&177     /GET NEXT BYTE
        RTR                     /MOVE TO LOW ORDER
        RTR                     /4 BITS OF WORD
        TAD     SPARM&177       /SHOVE IN OTHER PIECE
        DCA I   BT2PTR&177      /STORE INTO 07600
        ISZ     BT2PTR&177      /BUMP POINTER/COUNTER
        JMP     BT2LUP&177      /LOOP BACK
S437,   JMP I   S7600&177       /START THIRD PHASE

S14,    21-5                    /SECTOR-TRACK CONSTANT
        FIELD   1               /WHERE IT GENERATES

        *HSTART+400             /WHERE IT IS WRITTEN OUT FROM

        NOPUNCH                 /FOOL THE ASSEMBLER

        FIELD   HFIELD%10       /WHERE IT EXECUTES

        *SBOOT                  /LAST PAGE AGAIN

        ENPUNCH                 /UN-FOOL THE ASSEMBLER

/THE FOLLOWING CODE IS EXECUTED IN FIELD 0. IT MOVES ITSELF FROM 07600 TO H7600
/THEN RESUMES IN HFIELD SO THAT THE SYSTEM HANDLER CODE CAN BE MOVED TO 07600.

        NOPUNCH                 /FOOL THE ASSEMBLER

        FIELD   0               /THIS DOES A *200!

        *SBOOT                  /THIS CODE EXECUTES IN FIELD 0

        ENPUNCH                 /RESUME WITH BINARY

SBOOT,  TAD I   HFPTR           /MOVE HELPER FIELD
        CDF     HFIELD          /CONTENTS FROM 07600
        DCA I   HFPTR           /TO H7600, LENGTH
        CDF     00              /OF ONE PAGE
        ISZ     HFPTR           /FROM-POINTER, TO-POINTER, AND COUNTER!
        JMP     SBOOT           /GET IT ALL
        CIF     HFIELD          /WE MUST RESUME IN HFIELD
        JMP     SYSREST         /AS THIS WILL SOON BE DESTROYED

HFPTR,  SBOOT                   /WHERE THIS CODE IS NOW

        FOO=    .               /REMEMBER WHERE WE ARE

        NOPUNCH                 /FOOL THE ASSEMBLER AGAIN

        FIELD   HFIELD%10       /RESTORE FIELD SETTING

        *FOO                    /AND ORIGIN SETTING

        ENPUNCH                 /WE NOW RETURN CONTROL TO YOUR BINARY LOADER!
/THIS CODE IS ENTERED WHENEVER A WARM BOOTSTRAP IS PERFORMED. ITS PURPOSE IS TO
/RESTORE THE SYSTEM HANDLER CODE AND ACTUALLY STARTUP THE MONITOR.

HFIXUP, JMS     SYSFIX          /RESTORE 07600
        CIF     00              /TO FIELD 0
        JMP I   STKBM           /START IT UP

STKBM,  INPBUF                  /MONITOR STARTING ADDRESS AFTER LOADING

/THE FOLLOWING CODE IS EXECUTED IN FIELD HFIELD%10. IT FIRST MOVES THE SYSTEM
/HANDLER FROM 00000 (WHERE THE MANUAL BOOT LOADED IT) TO 07600 (STANDARD
/LOCATION). IT THEN RESTORES VITAL AREAS OF THE SYSTEM HANDLER TO THEIR
/DEFINED VALUES AND DOES A WARM BOOT.

SYSREST,TAD     S7600H          /RESET THE
        DCA     SYSPTR          /MOVING
        DCA     SYSFIX          /POINTERS
SYMVLP, TAD I   SYSFIX          /MOVE THE SYSTEM
        DCA I   SYSPTR          /HANDLER FROM 00000
        ISZ     SYSFIX          /TO 07600, LENGTH
        ISZ     SYSPTR          /OF ONE PAGE
        JMP     SYMVLP          /DO IT ALL
        JMS     SYSFIX          /SUBROUTINE TO RESTORE 07600
        CIF     00              /WARM START IN FIELD 0
        JMP     SBOOT           /STANDARD LOCATION

/TERMINATE TRANSFER AND CHECK FOR ERRORS SUBROUTINE.

STERM,  .-.                     /TERMINATE TRANSFER SUBROUTINE
        TAD     S603            /MAKE A TERMINATE COMMAND
        SFWR                    /ISSUE IT
        JMS     SWAIT           /WAIT FOR CRC AVAILABILITY
        SFRD                    /603 STILL IN AC!
        AND     S110            /ONLY CRC ERROR + FAULT
        CIF     00              /WHERE WE WERE CALLED FROM
        JMP I   STERM           /RETURN TO SENDER

/WAIT FOR DATA-SERVICE FLAG SUBROUTINE.

        IFNZRO  SYSIO-.         <ERROR  .>
SWAIT,  .-.                     /WAIT FOR  DATA SERVICE FLAG
        SFSF                    /SKIP IOT
        JMP     .-1             /WAIT A LONG TIME
        JMP I   SWAIT           /THAT'S IT
/THIS SUBROUTINE DOES THE WORK OF RESTORING THE SYSTEM
/HANDLER FOR USE BY THE OUTSIDE WORLD.

SYSFIX, .-.                     /MUST CONTAIN 0 FOR COLD BOOTSTRAP
        CDF     00              /DATA FIELD IS RANDOM
        DCA I   PSBBLK          /BLOCK 0
        TAD     SBJMS           /GET THE JMS INSTRUCTION
        DCA I   S7600H          /RESTORE IT
        JMP I   SYSFIX          /EXIT TO CALLER

PSBBLK, SBOOT+3                 /SBOOT BLOCK ARGUMENT

/THIS SUBROUTINE GETS A WORD FROM THE SYSTEM DEVICE, PRESERVING THE LINK ACROSS
/CALLS (FOR THE BENEFIT OF THE SLURP LOADER).

SGETWD, .-.                     /GET A WORD SUBROUTINE
        CLA RAL                 /SAVE THE LINK
        DCA     STERM           /IN A TEMPORARY
        JMS     SWAIT           /WAIT ON THE FLAG
        SFRD                    /READ DATA BYTE
        CLL RTL                 /MOVE TO HIGH ORDER
        RTL                     /EIGHT BITS OF WORD
        DCA     SPUTWD          /ANOTHER TEMP
        JMS     SWAIT           /WAIT FOR LAST ONE TO FINISH
        SFRD                    /READ IT IN ALSO
        RTR                     /MOVE H.O. 4 BITS
        RTR                     /INTO L.O. 4 BITS
        TAD     SPUTWD          /(OTHER 4 BITS ARE CLEAN)
        DCA     SPUTWD          /VOILA, A 12-BIT WORD!
        TAD     STERM           /RESTORE READ/WRITE
S110,   CLL RAR                 /STATUS FOR LOOP
        TAD     SPUTWD          /GET THE WORD
        CIF     00              /BACK TO FIELD 0
        JMP I   SGETWD          /EXIT TO CALLER

/THIS SUBROUTINE WRITES A WORD TO THE SYSTEM DEVICE (TRANSFER INITIATED ELSEWHERE).

SPUTWD, .-.                     /WRITE A WORD SUBROUTINE
        CLL RTR                 /MOVE OVER
        RTR                     /A HALF-BYTE
SBJMS,  JMS     SWAIT           /WAIT FOR THE FIFO
        SFWR                    /WRITE IT
        RAR                     /RECOVER THAT BIT!
        AND     S7600H          /CLEAN EXTRANEOUS STUFF
        CLL RTR                 /BIT 3 MUST BE 0!
        RTR                     /MOVE INTO HIGH-ORDER 4 BITS OF BYTE
        JMS     SWAIT           /WAIT A WHILE
        SFWR                    /WRITE IT OUT
S7600H, CLA+400                 /CLEANSE OURSELVES
        CIF     00              /WE WERE CALLED FROM FIELD 0
        JMP I   SPUTWD          /EXIT TO WHOEVER
BIFIN,  SZA                     /ANY ERRORS?
        JMP     BIBARF          /BARF
        JMS     SYSFIX          /I FINISH-UP
        CIF     00              /BACK TO FIELD 0
        JMP     BICIF           /EXIT TO HIS CODE (ULTIMATELY)

BIBARF, HLT                     /FATAL ERROR
        JMP     BIBARF          /TOUGH!

S603,   603                     /CONSTANT 0603
SYSPTR, SBOOT                   /RESTORE POINTER

/       IOT DEFINITIONS:

        SFWR=   6321            /OUTPUT COMMAND OR DATA
        SFSF=   6322            /SKIP ON DATA SERVICE FLAG
        SFRD=   6324            /READ DATA OR STATUS
        XLIST   OFF     >
        XLIST   OFF
        IFNZRO  TC01    <
        XLIST   ON
/TC01-TC08 DECTAPE SYSTEM HANDLER
SBOOT,  JMS     SYSIO           /CALL I/O ROUTINES TO BOOT
S7600,  7600                    /READ INTO 7600
S200,   0200                    /THIS IS PARTIALLY IGNORED
        0000                    /BLOCK 0
SWAL,   .-.                     /SWITCHES /A-/L
SWMX,   .-.                     /SWITCHES /M-/X
SWY9,   .-.                     /SWITCHES /Y-/9
SOUTFLS,.-.                     /NUMBER OF OUTPUT FILES
SDATE,  .-.                     /SYSTEM DATE WORD
SCRSIZE,.-.                     /SOFTWARE CORE SIZE
 
SCOM,   SHERE                   /SYSIO WAIT ROUTINE
        DTXA                    /DO PASSED FUNCTION
        TAD     S7600           /SETUP FOR
        DCA     SWC             /200 WORDS
        DTSF DTRB               /WAIT FOR DECTAPE
        JMP     .-1             /OR ERROR FLAG
        RTL                     /CHECK FOR
S7750,  SPA SNA CLA             /END ZONE ERROR?
        JMP     STURNX          /YES, GO DO A TURNAROUND
        DTRB                    /CHECK FOR
        SMA                     /REAL ERRORS?
        JMP I   SCOM            /NO, RETURN NORMALLY
SERR,   HLT                     /COMPLAIN ABOUT ERRORS
        JMP     SRETRY          /TRY, TRY AGAIN

S10,    10                      /CONSTANT 0010
SCIF,   CIF CDF 00              /IN-LINE CODE CONSTANT
 
SLOAD,  JMS     SYSIO           /SYSTEM LOADER HAS DEFAULTS TO SAVE CORE
SCORE,  0                       /CORE ARGUMENT
SFUN,   WRITE                   /NUMBER OF BLOCKS TO READ OR WRITE, FIELD, UNIT
SBLOCK, BINADR                  /STARTING BLOCK NUMBER
        JMP I   .+1             /START AT
SYSTART,SBOOT                   /THIS STARTING ADDRESS
/I/O ROUTINES ENTER HERE
SYSIO,  INPBUF-1                /I/O ENTRY
        STA                     /-1
        TAD I   SYSIO           /ADD ON CURRENT ADDRESS VALUE
        DCA     SADDR           /SAVE AS TRANSFER ADDRESS FOR LATER
        RDF                     /WHO'S CALLING US?
        TAD     SCIF            /SETUP FOR GOING
        DCA     SOUT            /BACK TO THEM LATER
        ISZ     SYSIO           /BUMP TO NEXT ARGUMENT
        TAD I   SYSIO           /GET FUNCTION WORD
        DCA     SFUNCT          /SAVE IT
        ISZ     SYSIO           /BUMP TO BLOCK ARGUMENT
        TAD I   SYSIO           /GET DESIRED BLOCK
        STL CIA                 /INVERT IT
        TAD     STEM            /ADD ON CURRENT BLOCK
        TAD     SOVSHT          /AND OVERSHOOT FACTOR
SRETRY, STA CML                 /COMPLEMENT DIRECTION WITH NEXT
        TAD     S10             /AC=7, LINK=.NOT.LINK
        AND     SFUNCT          /GET UNIT BITS
        RTR                     /MOVE UNITS AND COMPLEMENTED
        RTR                     /DIRECTION TO BITS [0-3]
        TAD     S10             /ADD ON SEARCH BIT
        DTLA                    /LOAD REGISTER, STILL NO GO AND WRONG DIRECTION
        DTLB                    /SEARCH IN FIELD 0
        TAD I   SYSIO           /GET DESIRED BLOCK AGAIN
        DCA     STEM            /MAKE IT CURRENT BLOCK
        TAD     S7750           /SETUP CURRENT ADDRESS
        DCA     SCAA            /FOR SEARCHING
STURNX, NL4000                  /FORM A GO BIT
SCONT,  CML RTR                 /INVERT DIRECTION IN LINK AND
        RTR                     /MOVE TO BIT[3-4]
        JMS     SCOM            /GO GET A BLOCK
        DTRA                    /GET DIRECTION
        CMA RTL                 /COMPLEMENT IT AND
        RTL                     /MOVE IT TO LINK
        SNL CLA                 /GOING BACKWARDS?
        CML RTL                 /YES, ADD OVERSHOOT FACTOR
        TAD     SBLK            /GET CURRENT BLOCK
        CML CIA                 /INVERT FOR COMPARISON
        TAD     STEM            /ADD ON DESIRED BLOCK
        SNA CLA                 /SKIP NEXT IF WRONG BLOCK
        SNL CLA                 /SKIP NEXT IF GOING FORWARD ON RIGHT BLOCK
        JMP     SCONT           /GO BACK, LINK TELLS WHAT TO DO NEXT

/AT THIS POINT THE TAPE IS POSITIONED CORRECTLY FOR TRANSFERRING
 
        TAD     SADDR           /NOW SETUP
        DCA     SCAA            /CURRENT ADDRESS
        TAD     SFUNCT          /SETUP
        DTLB                    /TRANSFER FIELD
        TAD     SFUNCT          /GET FUNCTION, PAGE BITS
        RAL                     /FUNCTION GOES TO LINK
        AND     S7600           /JUST PAGE BITS IN AC
        DCA     SPGCNT          /SAVE THEM
        RAL                     /MOVE R/W TO AC BIT [11]
        IAC                     /AC=1 OR 2
        STL RTL                 /AC=6 OR 12
        RTL                     /AC=30 OR 50
SNEXT,  JMS     SCOM            /WAIT FOR 1 BLOCK TO BE TRANSFERRED
SHERE,  ISZ     STEM            /ACCOUNT FOR IT
        STL CLA                 /CLEAN UP;SET LINK IN CASE LAST
        TAD     SPGCNT          /GET PAGE COUNT
        TAD     S7600           /DECREMENT BY ONE PAGE
        SNA                     /DONE?
        JMP     SEXIT           /YES, EXIT
        DCA     SPGCNT          /NO, SAVE UPDATED COUNT
        JMP     SNEXT           /GO DO ANOTHER
SEXIT,  TAD     S200            /STOP THE
        DTXA                    /TAPE DRIVE
        ISZ     SYSIO           /BUMP TO FINAL POSITION
SOUT,   CIF CDF 00              /INITIALIZED IN CASE OF DATA FIELD PROBLEMS
        JMP I   SYSIO           /RETURN TO CALLER
 
SOVSHT, 10                      /CHANGE THIS FOR INSTALLATIONAL OPTIMUM
STEM,   .-.                     /LATEST BLOCK NUMBER HERE
SADDR,  .-.                     /TRANSFER ADDRESS

        ZBLOCK  7750-.          /EMPTY SPACE

        IFNZRO  7750-.  <ERROR  .>
SBLK,   .-.                     /BLOCK NUMBERS GO HERE
SPGCNT, 20^200                  /READ IN BLOCKS 0-17 FOR BOOTSTRAP
SFUNCT, 20^100                  /FUNCTION TEMPORARY

        ZBLOCK  7754-.          /EMPTY SPACE

        IFNZRO  7754-.  <ERROR  .>
SWC,    SCAA                    /WORD COUNT

        IFNZRO  7755-.  <ERROR  .>
SCAA,   SCAA                    /CURRENT ADDRESS
SPARM,  .-.                     /PASSED EQUALS PARAMETER
SFILES, ZBLOCK  -.              /PASSED FILE ARGUMENTS

/       DECTAPE SYMBOLS

        DTCA=   6762            /CLEAR DECTAPE "A" REGISTER
        DTLA=   6766            /LOAD DECTAPE "A" REGISTER
        DTLB=   6774            /LOAD DECTAPE "B" REGISTER
        DTRA=   6761            /READ DECTAPE "A" REGISTER
        DTRB=   6772            /READ DECTAPE "B" REGISTER
        DTSF=   6771            /SKIP ON DECTAPE FLAG OR ERROR FLAG
        DTXA=   6764            /XOR DECTAPE "A" REGISTER
        XLIST   OFF             >
